# results: new game -> licence -> race -> RACE OVER -> race-results screen.
#
# Needs a long RUN_SECS: run as
#   make docker-test SCENARIO=results SECS=220
# (RUN_SECS=220 -> keys bound = RUN_SECS+30 = 250s; run.sh's own host
# watchdog is RUN_SECS+120 = 340s, comfortably above both).
#
# Reuses race.keys's path to a running race (see race.keys for that half),
# then waits out an AI-only race and screenshots the results screen that
# shows all four finishing cars' colours (the 521609e car-palette
# question). Measured:
# AI-only races take 90-139s once running; this waits 155s for margin, then
# 0-1 tracks worth of slack before RUN_SECS would stop the container.
#
# shot:licence and shot:race are extra checkpoints in
# addition to shot:results.
#
# Post-race navigation: postRaceMain draws easyRaceResults() first (no key
# needed - it runs as soon as the race-over condition is detected), which
# already draws the four finishing cars via drawRightPositions/sub_424240
# (ui/raceResultsScreen.c) - the exact function 521609e touched. So this
# scenario does not need the down/down/down/down navigation once used to
# reach the shop; the very first results screen is already the target.
# The one `enter` sent after the wait is a no-op if postRaceMain already
# auto-triggered (Enter was found to be ignored on these screens, only
# certain other keys advance them) and dismisses "RACE OVER" if a keypress
# was in fact needed - safe either way.
#
# Works for both our exe and the original dr.exe (make docker-test ORIG=1
# SCENARIO=results) when the menu timing matches closely enough for the
# same wait values; results-orig.keys exists because it does not.
enter w3500
shot:menu
enter w1500
enter w1500
t w200
e w200
s w200
t w200
enter w1200
shot:licence
enter w1500
enter w3000
enter w2500
enter w20000
enter w2000
shot:race
w155000
enter w4000
shot:results
